      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 326.42,
      "end_seconds": 360.93,
      "duration_seconds": 34.51,
      "text": "it's reasonable to be concerned, but right now perimenopause is my leading thought, not anything worse let's book a thyroid test to look into hot flushes i want a blood count done, that's for irregular periods for this, estradiol gel, 1 pump, once a day, long term that's for menopausal symptoms regular exercise, light layers and avoiding triggers can help please take the tablets with food so they don't upset your stomach"
